#966 is fixed for text-only runs, where the model calls no tools: --print and --output-format json now write the answer to stdout exactly once. One leak remains: when tools run, their progress lines still go to stdout (details at the end).

What changed
• There's a new process-wide flag, "stdout is reserved for the final payload", in src/format/mod.rs. src/main.rs sets it for --print or JSON output, on both the -p path and the piped-input path. JSON counts whether you use --json or --output-format json.
• All 14 places in src/prompt.rs that stream answer text (the text itself, markdown flushes and the newlines around it) now go through write_stream_text, which writes nothing when the flag is set. That leaves emit_output as the only thing writing the answer. The terminal bell is skipped in these modes too.
• `-o <file>, the REPL and plain -p` behave as before.

Tests
• Flag set: the streamed text writes nothing.
• Flag unset: output is byte-for-byte what it was.
• A source check fails if the number of gated write sites changes or a bare print! of the streamed text comes back. It only proves the gate is in the code, not that it fires.
• `reserves_stdout is tested for --print` and JSON separately, so neither test can pass because of the other.
• The tests pass the flag in as a parameter rather than flipping the global, so parallel tests can't interfere.

Manual check against a small local stub server (--no-tools --max-turns 1):

| Mode | Before | After |
|---|---|---|
| --print | \n{"answer": 42}\n\n{"answer": 42} (from the assessment's run) | {"answer": 42}, 14 bytes, no leading blank line |
| -p … --output-format json | streamed text, then the envelope (jq fails with "Extra data") | one object, accepted by python3 -m json.tool |
| piped input, JSON | same leak | one object, parses |
| plain -p | — | still streams as before |

The "before" row is the assessment's recorded output; I didn't rebuild the old binary to re-run it.

cargo fmt -- --check, cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings and the full cargo test suite all passed. I added a CHANGELOG line and a note in docs/src/usage/piped-mode.md. prompt.rs is about 60 lines over its size-gate entry, still inside the 100-line allowance.

Still open: when a run calls tools, the tool-progress lines (▶ summary, ✓/✗, batch summaries, diffs, turn boundaries) still print to stdout. So --print and JSON output are only clean for runs that call no tools. This task only covered the answer-text writes, so I left those lines alone and noted the gap in the docs. Fixing it means sending that output to stderr (or suppressing it) when stdout is reserved, and it should be a follow-up issue.
